<!-- INTRODUCTION -->

<h2 style="text-align:center; color:#c77dff; font-size:220%;">
    WHAT IS THE FUTURE OF SPEED?
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    When we hear the word <b>speed</b>, we often think about how fast
    a car can travel. But speed is much more than a number.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    A fast car needs a powerful engine, strong brakes, good tyres,
    advanced aerodynamics and technology that helps the driver
    control the car.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Over the years, engineers have discovered new ways to make
    cars faster, safer, lighter and more efficient.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The Porsche 911 and BMW M4 are excellent examples of this
    evolution. One has a history stretching back to the 1960s.
    The other grew from BMW's famous motorsport programme.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    To understand the future of speed, we first need to understand
    the history that created these two legendary performance cars.
</p>

