    width="650">
</p>


<h2 style="color:#ff3333;">
    6. THE 911 TURBO
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Porsche later introduced turbocharging to the 911 family.
    The first production 911 Turbo became known internally
    as the <b>930</b>.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Turbocharging allowed engineers to produce much more power
    from the engine.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The Turbo also became famous for its large rear spoiler,
    wide body and dramatic performance.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The 911 Turbo helped establish the idea that Porsche could
    combine everyday usability with extreme performance.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#ff3333;">
    7. THE EIGHT GENERATIONS OF THE 911
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The Porsche 911 has passed through eight major generations.
</p>

<p style="text-align:center; font-size:130%; color:#ff5555;">
    <b>
        Original 911 → G-Series → 964 → 993 →
        996 → 997 → 991 → 992
    </b>
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Each generation introduced new technology, new engineering
    solutions and improved performance.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    However, Porsche continued to make the car recognizable
    as a 911.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#ff3333;">
    8. THE 964 — A MAJOR TECHNOLOGY STEP
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The <b>964</b> generation arrived in 1989.
    A large amount of the car was newly developed.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The 964 introduced important technologies including
    <b>all-wheel drive</b>, airbags and Tiptronic transmission.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The Carrera used a 3.6-litre boxer engine producing
    around 250 PS.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#ff3333;">
    9. THE 993 — THE END OF AN ERA
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The <b>993</b> generation introduced a new multi-link
    rear axle that improved the driving characteristics.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    It also became famous because it was the
    <b>last air-cooled generation</b> of the 911.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The 993 Turbo used twin-turbo technology and demonstrated
    how far Porsche had developed the 911.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#ff3333;">
    10. THE 996 — WATER COOLING
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The <b>996</b> brought one of the biggest technological
    changes in 911 history.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Porsche moved from the traditional air-cooled engine
    to <b>water cooling</b>.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    This change helped Porsche meet modern performance and
    emissions requirements.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#ff3333;">
    11. THE 997 — TECHNOLOGY MEETS TRADITION
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The <b>997</b> generation brought back the classic
    round-headlight appearance.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Porsche introduced technologies such as
    <b>Porsche Active Suspension Management</b>.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Later models also received advanced dual-clutch
    transmission technology.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#ff3333;">
    12. THE 991 — LIGHTER AND SMARTER
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The <b>991</b> generation introduced a new body structure
    using aluminium and steel.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    It also brought technologies such as rear-wheel steering,
    active aerodynamics and advanced chassis systems.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#ff3333;">
    13. THE 992 — THE MODERN 911
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The <b>992</b> is the eighth generation of the Porsche 911.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    It combines the traditional six-cylinder boxer engine
    with modern electronics and advanced driver technology.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Modern 911 technology includes systems such as
    wet-road detection, night vision and advanced aerodynamics.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Porsche has also introduced hybrid technology into the
    911 family, showing that the traditional sports car
    can continue to evolve.
</p>

