<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The <b>BMW M1</b> became another important milestone
    in BMW M history.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    It was a mid-engined sports car developed with
    BMW Motorsport involvement.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#4da6ff;">
    5. THE BMW M3
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    In <b>1986</b>, BMW introduced the first-generation M3.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The M3 became one of the most important performance
    cars in BMW history.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The idea was to bring motorsport-inspired performance
    into a road-going car.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#4da6ff;">
    6. WHY DID BMW CREATE THE M4?
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    In <b>2014</b>, BMW changed the naming system for its
    performance coupe.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The four-door performance sedan continued to be called
    the <b>M3</b>, while the coupe became the <b>M4</b>.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The new name gave the coupe its own identity while
    preserving its connection to the M3 family.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#4da6ff;">
    7. THE FIRST BMW M4
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The first BMW M4 appeared in 2014.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    It used a turbocharged six-cylinder engine and
    BMW M TwinPower Turbo technology.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The M4 combined high performance with the ability
    to be used as a road car.
</p>

