<h1 style="text-align:center; color:#c77dff;">
    PORSCHE 911 VS BMW M4
</h1>

<h2 style="text-align:center;">
    TWO DIFFERENT IDEAS OF PERFORMANCE
</h2>

<h2 style="color:#ff3333;">
    PORSCHE 911 — THE ICON
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The Porsche 911 represents more than six decades of
    continuous sports-car development.
</p>

<h2 style="color:#4da6ff;">
    BMW M4 — THE ATHLETE
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The BMW M4 represents modern BMW M performance,
    with roots deeply connected to motorsport.
</p>

<h2 style="color:#c77dff;">
    HISTORY
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    <b style="color:#ff5555;">Porsche 911:</b>
    Began with the 901 in 1963 and continued through
    eight generations.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    <b style="color:#4da6ff;">BMW M4:</b>
    The M4 name appeared in 2014, but its roots go back
    through BMW Motorsport and the M3.
</p>

<h2 style="color:#c77dff;">
    ENGINEERING
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The 911 became famous for its rear-engine boxer layout
    and its continuous evolution.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The M4 developed from BMW's motorsport philosophy,
    combining engine performance, chassis engineering,
    aerodynamics and driver control.
</p>

<h2 style="color:#c77dff;">
    DESIGN
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The 911 has kept a recognizable silhouette for generations.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The M4 uses a more modern and aggressive BMW M design language.
</p>

<h2 style="color:#c77dff;">
    PERSONALITY
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The 911 feels like an evolving piece of sports-car history.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The M4 feels like a modern performance machine
    connected to BMW's racing culture.
</p>


