<h2 style="color:#4da6ff;">
    10. THE FUTURE OF BMW M
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    BMW M also faces a major question about the future of
    performance cars.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    If performance cars become more electric, connected
    and intelligent, BMW M will need to preserve the
    emotional experience of an M car.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Future M cars could combine electric power,
    advanced software, lightweight materials,
    artificial intelligence and motorsport technology.
</p>


<h2 style="color:#c77dff;">
    11. WHAT WILL A CAR KNOW IN THE FUTURE?
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    A future car might understand:
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    <b>
        • Where it is<br>
        • What the road looks like<br>
        • How fast nearby vehicles are travelling<br>
        • Whether the road is wet<br>
        • Where traffic is building up<br>
        • Whether there are hazards ahead<br>
        • Which route may be safer
    </b>
</p>


<h2 style="color:#c77dff;">
    12. WHAT WILL THE NEXT GENERATION IMAGINE?
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Today's children may grow up with technologies that
    seem impossible today.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    They may imagine cars that communicate, think,
    fly, drive themselves or travel into environments
    where today's cars cannot go.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    The engineers of tomorrow may be the children who
    are imagining these ideas today.
</p>

