<h2 style="color:#c77dff;">
    13. WHAT WILL "SPEED" MEAN TOMORROW?
</h2>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    Today, speed is usually measured in kilometres per hour.
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    But future speed could mean much more:
</p>

<p style="font-size:120%; color:#e8edf7;">
    <b>
        Faster reactions.<br>
        Faster communication.<br>
        Faster charging.<br>
        Faster computing.<br>
        Faster navigation.<br>
        Faster decision-making.
    </b>
</p>

<p style="text-align:center; font-size:145%; color:#c77dff;">
    <b>
        THE FASTEST CAR MAY NOT ALWAYS BE
        THE CAR WITH THE HIGHEST TOP SPEED.
    </b>
</p>


